From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm: TF_GLM_KDA_PAD pads the KDA input stack at one width

ai-engine 917575463..e796315f3, squashed. TP=3 splits KDA heads 22/21/21, so the fused input
row width is 8,726 / 8,341: not a multiple of 8, which makes glm_mm skip the stack and cost about
9 ms a call. With the knob on, the stack is copied to its own eight-aligned buffer (true rows,
then zeros) so it packs; the pad columns come from zero weights and are ignored, and the field
offsets inside a row do not move. `tileLinears` calls it at load, so the pad applies to a stack
only when the knob is set.

Receipt (ai-engine, measured on the dev triangle): padded at 4 dense bits, decode aggregate
tok/s 46.12/46.14 to 58.88/58.29 at one stream, 63.01/62.85 to 72.80/72.66 at two, 70.73/69.77
to 79.24/79.11 at four, 79.07/79.62 to 84.92/85.55 at six, 85.97 to 89.75/89.72 at eight: no
regression at any level. Numerics: the pad columns are exactly zero (0 of 68 dumped), but at
DENSE_BITS=4 the stack is quantized where it was not before, so replies differ; the accuracy
gate that cleared it is the retrieval fixture, not bit-identity. Default off.

Gate: applies on the pin; check-native-cuda-host green; whole-tree fmt green; lean base-vs-head
0 new; the pad's own check rides in the patch.

Folded in by the 2026-11-12 fold (work/fold/MAP.tsv), each hunk where it belongs:
- 0024: tileLinears calls padKdaInputs again, the KDA_DUMP hook moves into it, the staged download is back
- 0040: cuda_state rows take rowWidth's one common padded width, and padKdaInputs is called once
- 0041: tileLinears synchronizes before the read-back; its restore of prompt_pair.wanted's TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO argument cancels the port's own change, so cuda_engine.zig is untouched here

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- TF_GLM_KDA_PAD, its padWidth and the one common rowWidth are the pin's own and v1.2.7's (cuda_ranks.zig:65, cuda_kda_block.zig:37-60): what this lever still adds is the TF_GLM_KDA_DUMP hook.
- lean_check.py's DIRECT_GETENV: TF_GLM_KDA_DUMP is a .glm .path row read by environment.path through profile.lookup, not std.c.getenv; cuda_env_test.zig lists it among GLM's own readers.
- Dropped, each an old-0003 port artifact a later old patch undid: body()'s 13-argument bodyProfile call (bodyProfile still takes 14 at v1.2.7) and the o_site fork moved above project (old 0041 put it back).
- Dropped: the docstring swap on padKdaInputs (the fold's text describes linears()), the trailing comment on the staged download and the check's reworded doc line; none changes behaviour.
- 5b80e93ac moved the KDA chain to zig/src/cuda/kda.zig (cuda_kda_block.zig now `const kda = cuda.kda`); the hook sits in project(), which that commit left in place.
- source: work/fold/0006-kda-pad-one-width.patch

